Subject: [PATCH] Let a PowerDNS CNAME name a target outside its zone

lexicon qualified every CNAME target into the zone that it wrote, even one
with a trailing dot, and qualified every target that it read back.  So a
CNAME in one zone could not name a target in another.  A target with its
trailing dot now stays absolute, and a target read back loses only its dot.

---
--- a/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/lexicon/_private/providers/powerdns.py
+++ b/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/lexicon/_private/providers/powerdns.py
@@ -163,7 +163,8 @@
                 content = '"' + content
             if content[-1] != '"':
                 content += '"'
-        elif rtype == "CNAME":
+        elif rtype == "CNAME" and not content.endswith("."):
+            # A target with its trailing dot is absolute, and can be outside the zone.
             content = self._fqdn_name(content)
         return content
 
@@ -171,7 +172,8 @@
         if rtype in ("TXT", "LOC"):
             content = content.strip('"')
         elif rtype == "CNAME":
-            content = self._full_name(content)
+            # PowerDNS answers with the absolute name, which can be outside the zone.
+            content = content.rstrip(".")
         return content
 
     def create_record(self, rtype, name, content):
